<SEOPage title="Hide other variant images in Shopify | VariantLens" description="Hide product images that do not belong to the currently selected Shopify variant while keeping assignments under merchant control." eyebrow="Cleaner product pages" heading="Hide images from other Shopify variants" intro="When a shopper chooses one colour, keep the gallery focused on that colour rather than every option in the product."><h2>The problem with one combined gallery</h2><p>A combined gallery can make it difficult to tell which photograph belongs to the selected colour. This is especially noticeable on products with several views for every option.</p><h2>Hide by assignment, not by filename</h2><p>VariantLens stores the media choices you make for each variant. That means the display rule comes from an explicit assignment rather than assumptions about image filenames or ordering.</p><h2>Shared images can still be used</h2><p>If a size chart, material close-up, or care image belongs to several variants, it can be assigned wherever it is relevant.</p><h2>Test the result in your theme</h2><p>Theme galleries differ, so every configured product should be checked on desktop and mobile. If a theme cannot be integrated safely, its existing gallery should remain available rather than being hidden prematurely.</p></SEOPage>

